  "steps": [
    {
      "step_id": "tile_data_shape_and_types.s01",
      "type": "explainer",
      "concept_ids": [
        "data.dataset_rows_columns"
      ],
      "eyebrow": "DATASETS AND VARIABLE TYPES",
      "title": "A dataset is a collection of observations",
      "lede": "Northstar Store wants to understand its orders better, so it starts by looking at how the data is laid out.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Northstar records every delivery the same way: an order number, the city it went to, which driver handled it and how long it took. All those orders, each written down with the same set of details, form what analysts call a dataset -- a collection of observations recorded on the same set of variables.",
          "role": "intro",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb1"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#f1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "data_table",
          "asset_ref": {
            "asset_id": "northstar_orders",
            "variant_id": null,
            "columns": [
              "order_id",
              "customer_segment",
              "city",
              "driver",
              "items",
              "order_value_ngn",
              "delivery_minutes"
            ]
          },
          "caption": "Northstar's delivery orders, one order per line.",
          "inspect": {
            "enabled": true,
            "caption_template": "For order {order_id}, {column} = {value}.",
            "id_column": "order_id"
          },
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns"
            ],
            "anchors": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#visual"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Analysts most often keep a dataset as a table -- sometimes called a data matrix -- made of rows and columns: a grid where every order has its own line and every detail about an order has its own column.",
          "role": "definition",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb2"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#f2"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "lineage": {
        "concept_ids": [
          "data.dataset_rows_columns"
        ],
        "teaching_block_ids": [
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb1",
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb2"
        ],
        "fact_ids": [
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#f1",
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#f2"
        ],
        "anchors": [
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#visual"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "step_id": "tile_data_shape_and_types.s02",
      "type": "explainer",
      "concept_ids": [
        "data.dataset_rows_columns"
      ],
      "eyebrow": "DATASETS AND VARIABLE TYPES",
      "title": "Rows and columns mean different things",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Every row is one observation",
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Each row represents one observation -- one record. In Northstar's table that means one row per order: NS1001 is one row, NS1002 is the next, and each is a separate delivery.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb3"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#f3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Every column is one variable",
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Each column represents one variable: one attribute recorded for every observation. The city column holds the destination city for every order, and delivery_minutes holds the delivery time for every order -- each column holds just one kind of information.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb3"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#f4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "That tells you how to read the table. Asked \"how many deliveries went to Lagos?\", you scan down the city column and count the matching rows. Asked \"what happened with order NS1004?\", you read across that one row. A row tells you about one delivery; a column tells you about one kind of fact across all deliveries.",
          "role": "example",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb4"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#f3",
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#f4"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "lineage": {
        "concept_ids": [
          "data.dataset_rows_columns"
        ],
        "teaching_block_ids": [
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb3",
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb4"
        ],
        "fact_ids": [
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#f3",
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#f4"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "step_id": "tile_data_shape_and_types.s03",
      "type": "check",
      "concept_ids": [
        "data.dataset_rows_columns"
      ],
      "title": "Check: what a column holds",
      "reward": {
        "gems": 5
      },
      "lineage": {
